{
 "title": "if let and while let",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "If you care about only one variant you can write **`if let`** instead of `match`: when the pattern matches, it is bound to the variable and the block runs, otherwise `else` runs."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "fn main():",
    "    maybe: Optional[i32] = Valid(42)",
    "    if let Valid(x) = maybe:",
    "        print(\"found\", x)",
    "    else:",
    "        print(\"nothing\")",
    "",
    "    none_here: Optional[i32] = None",
    "    if let Valid(y) = none_here:",
    "        print(\"found\", y)",
    "    else:",
    "        print(\"nothing\")"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "found 42",
    "nothing"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "**`while let`** loops as long as the pattern matches. `List.pop()` gives `Valid(element)` until it is empty, then `None`."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "fn main():",
    "    stack = List[str]()",
    "    stack.push(\"first\")",
    "    stack.push(\"second\")",
    "    stack.push(\"third\")",
    "    while let Valid(item) = stack.pop():",
    "        print(\"popped:\", item)"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "popped: third",
    "popped: second",
    "popped: first"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "exercise",
   "id": "c08-l05-x1",
   "prompt": "Use `while let` and `pop` to consume the numbers in the `nums` list and print their total.",
   "starter": [
    "fn main():",
    "    nums = List[i32]()",
    "    nums.push(4)",
    "    nums.push(5)",
    "    nums.push(6)",
    "    total = 0",
    "    print(total)"
   ],
   "solution": [
    "fn main():",
    "    nums = List[i32]()",
    "    nums.push(4)",
    "    nums.push(5)",
    "    nums.push(6)",
    "    total = 0",
    "    while let Valid(n) = nums.pop():",
    "        total += n",
    "    print(total)"
   ],
   "hint": "Do `total += n` inside `while let Valid(n) = nums.pop():`.",
   "expected": [
    "15"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "quiz",
   "id": "c08-l05-q1",
   "q": "When does `while let` stop?",
   "options": [
    "After 10 rounds",
    "When the pattern no longer matches (e.g. `pop()` gives `None`)",
    "Never"
   ],
   "answer": 1,
   "why": "The loop ends when the match fails."
  }
 ]
}
